* Recovered from 2277-alt/vinnix.lst (1992-09-23) and 6001/VINNIX.LST (1994-08-07).
* Those two include listings match. VINNIX.VDI/VINNIX.AH is not assembler source.
*
WDT	EQU	$8402
WDTMSK	EQU	8


* Stack Size

STACKLEN	EQU	$100

*
* MACRO DEFINITIONS
*

* CALL MACRO - USES SWI2 TO TRANSFER CONTROL TO
* CALLED FUNCTION. ARGUMENTS MUST BE PUSHED
* ONTO THE U-STACK BEFORE EACH CALL. THE
* MACRO PUSHU MAY BE USED TO ACCOMPLISH
* THIS IF THE ARGUMENTS ARE CONSTANTS.

TRAP   MACR
       SWI2
       FCB    \0
       ENDM

* MACRO TO DEFINE CODES FOR REAL TIME
* FUNCTIONS

SEQ    MACR
\0     EQU    COUNT
COUNT  SET    COUNT+1
       ENDM


COUNT  SET    0
       SEQ    SETRT
       SEQ    START
       SEQ    STARTV
       SEQ    WAITZ
       SEQ    WAIT
       SEQ    WAITE
       SEQ    ATTCH
       SEQ    WTWTO

RETURN MACR
       JMP    NEXT$
       ENDM


*
* RTEX
* real time executive for the 6809
*
* this executive is based on the 6800 real
* time executive supplied with motorola real
* time fortran.
*
* revision 1.0 by Caron Luk on June, 1989
* Added mpu option.
* Revision 1.1 By Caron Luk.
* 5/21/90 The system clock actually at 300.4807692Hz ((4MHz/416)/32)
*	  By requiring .5 p more every second, we are requiring 1661 
*	  more p every day.  To cancel these p, 1 p sub every min, 9 p
*	  every hour and 5 p every day, which sum up to 1661.  Now, the
*	  different is .538528 p /day, which is 196.56272 p / yr or 2/3 
*         of a sec slower.
*
* revision 1.1 by caron on June,1990
* Modified int1 such that board with reverse logic can use vinnix.asm.
* mask byte that with all LSBs set mean that ctr reg is in reverse logic
* interrupt bit clr when there is an interrupt request.  But the bit must 
* on the MSBs side, and RTEX will examine that ctr reg with the MSBs of 
* the mask, and transfer with the whole byte of the ctr reg to the handler
* if interrupt request is indicated.
*

